+// ========== Graphics context loss ==========
+
+// Registers |hwnd| to be notified, by a posted |message| with wParam and lParam
+// both zero, the first time the renderer's graphics context is permanently
+// lost. Pass a null |hwnd| to unregister.
+//
+// A context loss is the GPU going away underneath an otherwise healthy process
+// - a TDR, a driver reset or crash, an adapter change. This embedder has no
+// path that recreates the display or contexts afterwards, so the loss is
+// permanent: the rasterizer silently stops drawing while the engine continues
+// to report completed frames and the message loop keeps running. The window
+// therefore freezes with no other outward sign, and only restarting the process
+// recovers it.
+//
+// The message is posted, not sent, and is posted at most once per process. If
+// the context was already lost when this is called, the message is posted
+// immediately, so a late registration cannot miss the event.
+//
+// May be called from any thread.
+FLUTTER_EXPORT void FlutterDesktopSetGraphicsContextLostNotification(
+    HWND hwnd,
+    UINT message);
+
+// Returns true once the renderer's graphics context has been permanently lost.
+//
+// Never returns to false: see
+// |FlutterDesktopSetGraphicsContextLostNotification|. Provided for hosts that
+// prefer to poll rather than handle a message. May be called from any thread.
+FLUTTER_EXPORT bool FlutterDesktopIsGraphicsContextLost();
